WEBVTT

00:02.480 --> 00:05.860
<i>Next up, the weather.</i>

00:09.730 --> 00:13.470
<i>It sure is cold today. It's snowing everywhere!</i>

00:09.730 --> 00:20.490
Today's Weather

00:11.110 --> 00:12.150
Moto.

00:13.670 --> 00:17.690
Motoko, aren't you going
 to study with your friends?

00:14.320 --> 00:16.500
<i>Have you prepared for the cold weather?</i>

00:17.690 --> 00:19.220
Not until later.

00:19.220 --> 00:20.490
Oh, okay.

00:22.470 --> 00:24.790
Someone called yesterday.

00:25.590 --> 00:26.410
Huh?

00:26.410 --> 00:28.250
On the phone.

00:28.250 --> 00:29.470
It was a guy.

00:30.000 --> 00:32.980
He said his name was Kitahara.

00:32.980 --> 00:36.010
He asked for "Iura-san."

00:36.310 --> 00:38.960
But obviously, we're <i>all</i> Iuras.

00:38.960 --> 00:42.550
I... see...

00:43.310 --> 00:46.020
Why didn't you give the phone to me?

00:46.020 --> 00:47.710
I hung up.

00:48.270 --> 00:50.450
You idiot!

00:50.450 --> 00:52.280
Jeez. Pipe down, pipe down.

00:52.280 --> 00:54.400
Why'd you hang up on him?! 
Are you stupid?!

00:54.400 --> 00:57.060
You're supposed to pass the phone!
What is wrong with you?!

00:57.060 --> 01:00.660
Well, you were in the bath. 
And you went to bed early.

01:01.140 --> 01:03.690
So, you like this Kitahara guy?

01:03.690 --> 01:05.360
You don't even know him!

01:05.360 --> 01:07.420
And that's none of your business!

01:07.420 --> 01:09.620
He'd better not be a womanizer.

01:07.420 --> 01:14.050
<b>G
R
R
R
R
R</b>

01:09.620 --> 01:12.880
Don't bring him home when I'm not here.

01:12.880 --> 01:14.050
I wouldn't!

01:14.050 --> 01:20.100
K-K-Kitahara-kun has someone he likes.
And everyone knows it....

01:20.100 --> 01:21.530
<b>Fidget</b>

01:20.110 --> 01:23.800
They walk home from school together.

01:21.080 --> 01:22.290
<b>Fidget</b>

01:21.620 --> 01:23.040
<b>Fidget</b>

01:23.600 --> 01:25.000
<b>Shake</b>

01:23.800 --> 01:29.310
But the girl he likes 
a-already has a boyfriend!

01:24.370 --> 01:25.750
<b>Shake</b>

01:25.080 --> 01:26.540
<b>Shake</b>

01:25.830 --> 01:27.250
<b>Shake</b>

01:26.620 --> 01:28.020
<b>Shake</b>

01:27.370 --> 01:28.750
<b>Shake</b>

01:28.170 --> 01:29.320
<b>Shake</b>

01:28.830 --> 01:29.320
<b>Shake</b>

01:29.730 --> 01:32.850
So Kitahara-kun could...

01:38.180 --> 01:39.460
You done?

01:39.460 --> 01:42.990
Ugh... Yeah, I'm done.

01:43.440 --> 01:46.500
I wonder why Kitahara-kun called.

01:46.500 --> 01:50.550
Oh, he said to call off today's
study session if it snows.

01:50.550 --> 01:53.000
Why didn't you just tell me that, idiot?!

03:22.970 --> 03:26.470
Katagiri High School

03:27.270 --> 03:30.730
Please, no more English writing questions...

03:30.730 --> 03:34.230
Hori, I can't take any more...

03:34.570 --> 03:37.480
You'll both manage somehow.

03:37.480 --> 03:39.880
How can you say that?

03:39.880 --> 03:42.260
Did you take the English essay test, too?

03:42.260 --> 03:43.650
Yup, yup.

03:43.650 --> 03:46.990
We were talking about 
getting something to eat. You in?

03:46.990 --> 03:49.820
Heck yeah! You know I am!

03:50.750 --> 03:51.500
Checking for new messages

03:51.500 --> 03:58.250
New Message
<u>\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hFrom: Motoko</u>
You're coming home late, right?
My friend is coming over,
so things might get a little loud.
Take your time

03:52.030 --> 03:55.000
<i>You're coming home late, right?</i>

03:55.000 --> 03:58.250
<i>My friend is coming over, 
so things might get a little loud.</i>

03:58.600 --> 04:00.520
<i>Take your time.</i>

04:03.010 --> 04:09.270
<b>Iura</b>

04:03.520 --> 04:06.760
The tea is all set. Sweets, too.

04:07.300 --> 04:08.860
Now I just need to wait.

04:10.150 --> 04:12.910
Iura-san, are you doing 
anything after class?

04:12.910 --> 04:14.770
N-No.

04:15.120 --> 04:19.050
I heard we're applying to the same 
high school. Care to study together?

04:19.050 --> 04:21.850
It's supposed to be a great way to learn.

04:21.850 --> 04:23.150
Yeah, sure!

04:23.520 --> 04:27.530
Okay, I'll drop my stuff off at home
 and head over to your place.

04:29.120 --> 04:32.560
This is just a study session! 
What would I think it's anything else?!

04:32.560 --> 04:33.410
He's here!

04:34.350 --> 04:36.920
K-Kitahara-kun, come on in...

04:36.920 --> 04:41.420
Kitahara?!

04:41.790 --> 04:43.920
Wh-What in the world?

04:43.920 --> 04:46.630
You said you'd be be home late.

04:46.630 --> 04:49.740
I never said anything like that.

04:49.740 --> 04:53.060
And I never heard anything
 about Kitahara coming over.

04:53.060 --> 04:56.020
Grandpa! Lemme borrow your replica sword!

04:56.020 --> 04:57.310
Stop it!

04:57.560 --> 04:59.360
Huh? My replica sword?

04:59.360 --> 05:00.610
No, we don't need it!

05:00.610 --> 05:02.790
He's just coming over to study!

05:04.690 --> 05:07.820
So, what time's he coming? Pretty soon?

05:07.820 --> 05:11.600
R-Right after he drops off 
some stuff at his house.

05:11.600 --> 05:13.020
Hmm...

05:14.000 --> 05:15.960
Study in the living room.

05:15.960 --> 05:18.990
There's no telling what middle 
schoolers will try these days.

05:18.990 --> 05:20.960
Maybe I should call the police in advance.

05:20.960 --> 05:22.780
We don't live in the slums!

05:22.780 --> 05:25.470
Jeez! Why don't you get a girlfriend already?

05:25.470 --> 05:27.340
I can't stand you!

05:27.340 --> 05:30.530
You always come straight home!

05:30.530 --> 05:32.990
Believe me, I'd love a girlfriend.

05:31.970 --> 05:36.980
<b>Friends
a-flirting</b>

05:31.970 --> 05:36.980
<b>Hee
hee</b>

05:31.970 --> 05:36.980
<b>Heh
heh</b>

05:33.740 --> 05:36.440
The lovebirds I see every day 
make it even worse.

05:36.980 --> 05:39.680
Anyway, should I bring you some tea?

05:39.680 --> 05:41.980
Don't do anything! Stay out!

05:46.710 --> 05:48.070
Maybe she's not home.

05:51.900 --> 05:52.840
Iura-san?

05:52.840 --> 05:54.200
You'd better stay out!

05:54.640 --> 05:57.160
If you come into the living room,
 I'm running away from home!

05:57.160 --> 05:59.080
Stay in your room!

05:59.080 --> 06:02.750
If you're not getting up to anything, 
what's it matter if I'm there or not?

06:02.750 --> 06:04.210
You disappoint me!

06:04.210 --> 06:07.970
What kind of brother 
points a sword at his younger sister?!

06:07.970 --> 06:11.140
Then you put yours down!
It's dangerous, you hear me?!

06:11.140 --> 06:12.930
Excuse me...

06:15.780 --> 06:17.230
Hello...

06:18.100 --> 06:19.570
So you're Kitahara.

06:19.570 --> 06:21.650
Hey!

06:21.650 --> 06:24.790
Are you her older brother?

06:26.040 --> 06:27.250
Correct.

06:28.420 --> 06:29.810
Come in.

06:29.810 --> 06:32.630
Would you like some tea? It's all we have.

06:32.630 --> 06:34.030
Hey!

06:35.350 --> 06:39.160
I'm sorry, Kitahara-kun. 
He's just in a bit of a mood.

06:39.690 --> 06:42.100
<i>He's so cool!</i>

06:42.100 --> 06:43.790
Kitahara-kun?

06:43.790 --> 06:45.170
Kitahara-kun!

06:45.170 --> 06:46.170
Huh?

06:46.560 --> 06:48.500
Oh, what is it, Iura-san?

06:51.230 --> 06:53.180
Our tea is rather bitter.

06:54.130 --> 06:55.590
Just the way I like it!

06:56.840 --> 06:59.050
<i>What a jerk of a brother!</i>

07:02.920 --> 07:04.870
Kitahara-kun, you're back.

07:04.870 --> 07:07.950
Care for tea? It's all we have.

07:08.310 --> 07:09.950
I love tea.

07:10.330 --> 07:12.450
It's even more bitter than before.

07:12.450 --> 07:14.200
I'm up to the challenge.

07:14.200 --> 07:16.560
Okay, I'll go make some.

07:18.080 --> 07:21.580
S-Sorry, he's in a mood.

07:22.020 --> 07:25.270
Don't apologize. I'm the one imposing.

07:26.100 --> 07:27.960
How much older is he than you?

07:27.960 --> 07:30.590
Three years. He's a third
 year in high school.

07:30.590 --> 07:32.090
I see.

07:33.360 --> 07:34.860
Here's your tea.

07:34.860 --> 07:36.730
Can you not be so rough about it?!

07:36.730 --> 07:38.850
Th-Thank you.

07:43.590 --> 07:44.730
Hold it!

07:44.730 --> 07:47.730
Why are you getting comfortable?
 Get out, idiot!

07:47.730 --> 07:49.990
I-It's okay, Iura-san.

07:50.440 --> 07:51.930
Am I intruding?

07:51.930 --> 07:53.490
Of course not!

07:53.820 --> 07:55.990
There you have it, Little Sister.

07:55.990 --> 07:57.940
He's just being polite!

07:57.940 --> 08:01.810
No, he's not. Right, Kitahara?

08:01.810 --> 08:03.310
You don't know him at all!

08:06.260 --> 08:08.670
I'm really sorry, Kitahara-kun.

08:08.670 --> 08:12.200
He's usually not this obnoxious...

08:12.660 --> 08:15.390
Oh. Sorry, I wasn't listening.

08:15.390 --> 08:18.180
Not closely, I mean...

08:18.180 --> 08:19.390
Okay.

08:21.000 --> 08:22.270
And stay out!

08:22.270 --> 08:26.280
What, really? 
That's the living room, y'know?

08:30.800 --> 08:35.470
I don't understand Kitahara-kun...

08:35.470 --> 08:37.660
Neither do I.

08:38.210 --> 08:40.870
I think I'm even more lost than you are.

08:40.870 --> 08:44.290
H-How can you say that when 
you caused all of this?!

08:44.290 --> 08:47.540
Don't you realize it's all your fault?!

08:47.870 --> 08:48.990
Huh?

08:48.990 --> 08:51.920
How's it my fault, seaweed head?

08:51.920 --> 08:55.210
You're the seaweed head, you marimo!

08:55.210 --> 08:56.930
M-Marimo?!

08:56.930 --> 09:02.310
Give back the old Kitahara-kun...

09:01.070 --> 09:03.680
U-Uh... Sorry?

09:04.020 --> 09:07.120
So you're saying you 
don't like Kitahara anymore?

09:07.510 --> 09:09.310
I didn't say that.

09:09.770 --> 09:13.450
But lately, when Kitahara-kun
 starts talking to me,

09:13.450 --> 09:17.820
I get the feeling it's
 not me he's interested in.

09:17.820 --> 09:20.020
M-Motoko...

09:20.330 --> 09:26.020
H-H-He might be talking to me
 because I remind him of you.

09:26.020 --> 09:28.580
Has Kitahara really
 strayed so far in your mind?

09:28.580 --> 09:31.780
It wouldn't be so bad if I were cuter,

09:28.580 --> 09:36.590
<b>Get it from their mom</b>

09:31.780 --> 09:35.260
but I look too much like you to be cute!

09:34.410 --> 09:36.590
That's going too far! Apologize to Mom!

09:36.590 --> 09:38.410
And you don't need to worry!

09:38.410 --> 09:42.370
People at school are always
 saying how cute I am!

09:42.370 --> 09:43.600
You liar!

09:43.600 --> 09:46.660
That's why you haven't found
 even a single girlfriend!

09:46.660 --> 09:48.670
Why would I want multiple?!

09:49.100 --> 09:51.360
<b>Student Council</b>

09:49.930 --> 09:51.360
No, not cute at all.

09:53.850 --> 09:58.540
What would <i>you</i> say if a guy walked up
and asked you if he was cute?

09:58.540 --> 09:59.700
Did you hit your head?

09:59.700 --> 10:01.210
No, I'm fine.

10:01.210 --> 10:02.260
Really?

10:02.680 --> 10:04.370
It's just that...

10:04.760 --> 10:07.850
Motoko says it's my fault she's not cute.

10:07.850 --> 10:10.380
Hey, Motoko-chan's plenty cute.

10:10.380 --> 10:13.310
Thank you, Hori-san! I feel much better!

10:13.310 --> 10:15.540
I wasn't saying it to be nice.

10:16.580 --> 10:18.130
Why not try longer hair?

10:18.130 --> 10:19.730
What? Me?

10:19.730 --> 10:21.660
Your sister, obviously.

10:22.120 --> 10:24.390
It might give a different impression.

10:24.390 --> 10:27.950
Her hair gets unruly,
so she won't grow it out.

10:29.000 --> 10:32.400
I think her short hair is cute, though.

10:32.400 --> 10:34.650
Oh, are you talking about me?

10:34.650 --> 10:35.900
Or perhaps me?

10:35.900 --> 10:39.400
What's with that confident grin?
I was talking about a <i>girl</i> with short hair.

10:39.950 --> 10:43.000
Well, I guess it's a sensitive subject.

10:43.000 --> 10:46.590
I mean, she looks like Iura,
but Motoko-chan's cuter.

10:46.590 --> 10:48.180
Huh? What's wrong with me?!

10:48.180 --> 10:50.420
We're not talking about you.

10:50.420 --> 10:53.120
Well, that's how adolescence goes.

10:53.120 --> 10:55.670
And after adolescence comes estrus.

10:56.010 --> 10:58.420
Are you suggesting my sister's a dog?

10:58.810 --> 11:02.500
Humans don't have estrous cycles. Trust me.
 I got a high score on the health exam.

11:02.500 --> 11:03.930
I see!

11:03.930 --> 11:07.360
If we did, maybe we wouldn't have 
that declining birth rate problem.

11:07.800 --> 11:10.190
<i>I feel like this is a stupid conversation.</i>

11:10.190 --> 11:12.310
I'm still in my adolescence!

11:12.310 --> 11:15.950
People who're in adolescence 
don't go around insisting they are!

11:15.950 --> 11:18.660
Then I guess estrus is next for you.

11:18.660 --> 11:20.270
Fine by me!

11:20.840 --> 11:25.590
Maybe adolescence is why Motoko's 
been saying such weird things lately...

11:25.590 --> 11:26.700
Like what?

11:27.170 --> 11:30.210
That I should hurry up and 
hook up with Sengoku-san.

11:33.560 --> 11:38.270
Every time you or Miyamura message me,
 she asks if it's from a girl.

11:38.270 --> 11:41.890
Well, maybe it's because 
you call him Sengoku<i>-san</i>!

11:41.890 --> 11:43.640
She's just joshing you.

11:43.640 --> 11:45.220
Maybe.

11:45.920 --> 11:49.070
I think Ayasaki-san's more attractive
 than Sengoku-san, though.

11:49.070 --> 11:51.480
Well, you probably would.

11:51.880 --> 11:57.280
Say, when Motoko-chan was at our place, 
she told us about the person she likes.

11:57.280 --> 11:59.110
Maybe she's...

11:59.110 --> 12:02.740
projecting her feelings onto you?

12:03.530 --> 12:05.200
So, the thing is...

12:05.860 --> 12:09.750
The person Moto likes seems to like me.

12:13.730 --> 12:15.880
S-So your sister likes girls?

12:16.270 --> 12:17.380
No.

12:17.380 --> 12:21.210
S-So it's something like this?
Seems rather hard to believe.

12:17.380 --> 12:25.260
<b>Super simple chart</b>

12:17.380 --> 12:25.260
<b>Iura-kun</b>

12:17.380 --> 12:25.260
<b>A-kun (anon)</b>

12:17.380 --> 12:25.260
<b>Motoko-chan</b>

12:21.210 --> 12:25.260
Yeah, that's about the size of it.
Though it is rather hard to believe.

12:25.590 --> 12:27.540
I feel sorry for Motoko-chan.

12:27.540 --> 12:28.250
What about me?

12:28.250 --> 12:30.600
Stolen by her brother?
She must be a soulless husk.

12:30.600 --> 12:32.770
Don't make it sound like she's dead!

12:33.110 --> 12:34.620
And I didn't steal anything!

12:34.620 --> 12:36.920
What do you mean? 
You totally swiped him.

12:36.920 --> 12:40.530
It's not like that! I want nothing
 to do with this relationship!

12:40.890 --> 12:43.510
I like girls!

12:43.510 --> 12:47.530
Yelling that will only get you into
a different kind of trouble, Shu.

12:48.020 --> 12:51.290
What about Sengoku? 
How do you feel about him?

12:51.800 --> 12:54.770
Why are you pushing 
Sengoku-san on me, too?

12:55.290 --> 12:57.040
I like Sengoku-san, obviously!

12:57.620 --> 12:58.520
Huh?

12:59.250 --> 13:00.490
Oh, Sengoku-san!

13:00.490 --> 13:03.320
So, Iura likes girls <i>and</i> Sengoku?

13:03.320 --> 13:07.040
This is too much for me!
It's so complicated!

13:07.040 --> 13:11.060
Stop! Don't make things any more confusing!

13:12.650 --> 13:13.630
I'm sorry.

13:13.630 --> 13:16.160
Not you too, Sengoku-san. 
You'll hurt my feelings.

13:16.990 --> 13:19.740
Just go get a girlfriend, man.

13:19.740 --> 13:22.820
What am I supposed to do? Make one?

13:22.820 --> 13:27.070
Out of clay, maybe? Will she love me?

13:24.190 --> 13:27.070
<b>My girlfriend</b>

13:27.580 --> 13:29.650
Don't you have someone you're interested in?

13:29.650 --> 13:31.990
Maybe someone in your class?

13:31.990 --> 13:34.990
No, not really...

13:34.990 --> 13:37.460
<i>He seems just like a high schooler.</i>

13:37.460 --> 13:39.830
Um, what's going on?

13:39.830 --> 13:41.050
No idea.

13:44.190 --> 13:47.470
Aren't you going to school today?

13:54.430 --> 13:57.990
Just so you know,
I tried to wake you up before.

13:57.990 --> 13:59.480
Really?

13:59.480 --> 14:01.480
What did I do?

14:01.480 --> 14:04.540
You said, "I know" and went 
back under the covers.

14:04.540 --> 14:06.490
What's there to know?!

14:06.490 --> 14:08.430
Oh, do you want some breakfast?

14:08.430 --> 14:11.220
Don't suggest things that will 
definitely make me late!

14:11.890 --> 14:15.000
Mom says you need to eat
 at least a slice of toast.

14:15.000 --> 14:18.810
I'll take it to go. You should get going, too.

14:18.810 --> 14:19.630
Okay.

14:21.430 --> 14:22.580
I'm off!

14:24.360 --> 14:28.420
<i>It's my first time seeing someone actually
 run to school with toast in their mouth.</i>

14:32.510 --> 14:36.940
<i>Th-The toast is drying out my mouth.</i>

14:37.310 --> 14:40.090
<i>I can't eat and run at the same time.</i>

14:41.940 --> 14:43.520
I'll switch to walking...

14:47.750 --> 14:49.400
I'm gonna be late!

14:50.280 --> 14:52.280
SLAM

14:52.860 --> 14:55.820
I was running with toast in 
my mouth and ran into a boy!

14:55.820 --> 14:58.710
What if he's a handsome transfer student?!

14:58.710 --> 15:02.050
Yoshikawa-san. Yoshikawa-san, are you okay?

15:02.050 --> 15:03.550
It's me, Iura.

15:07.970 --> 15:10.880
Oh, it's you. Good morning.

15:10.880 --> 15:11.970
Good morning.

15:12.900 --> 15:14.620
Did you sleep in, too?

15:14.620 --> 15:17.160
Yeah, after staying up too long.

15:17.160 --> 15:20.220
We'll be late even if we run.

15:20.710 --> 15:22.670
I'm late! I'm late!

15:24.120 --> 15:27.550
Huh? Why are you walking so leisurely?

15:27.550 --> 15:30.050
What about you, eating an onigiri?

15:30.960 --> 15:33.490
Hate to break it to you, 
but we're all gonna be late.

15:33.490 --> 15:35.480
Aw, man.

15:35.480 --> 15:36.390
What's in that?

15:36.390 --> 15:37.580
Just salt.

15:37.970 --> 15:40.130
I'm late! I'm late!

15:40.580 --> 15:43.580
What are you guys doing? We need to hurry!

15:43.580 --> 15:44.580
Tea

15:43.580 --> 15:45.590
You stopped by a convenience store?!

15:46.010 --> 15:47.100
What's in that?

15:47.100 --> 15:48.430
It's a meat bun.

15:48.430 --> 15:51.550
Why does everybody yell about being late?

15:51.550 --> 15:52.590
Who knows?

15:53.020 --> 15:54.840
There's no morning assembly today, right?

15:54.840 --> 15:55.980
Nope.

15:55.980 --> 15:57.870
Let's just walk, then.

15:58.600 --> 16:01.350
Katagiri High School

16:05.220 --> 16:08.230
Oh? You're all here early.
Good morning.

16:08.230 --> 16:08.940
Huh?!

16:08.940 --> 16:10.340
I can't believe it!

16:10.340 --> 16:13.100
You're late, Sengoku?! That never happens!

16:13.100 --> 16:13.870
Huh?

16:14.480 --> 16:17.310
Third-years only have class
 in the afternoon today.

16:17.310 --> 16:19.450
I'm here early for a 
student council meeting.

16:19.450 --> 16:20.250
Huh?

16:20.250 --> 16:23.620
I-I think I remember hearing
 that in homeroom yesterday.

16:23.620 --> 16:27.070
If I'd only known, I could have 
put jam on my toast!

16:27.070 --> 16:29.000
What's gotten into you four?

16:29.330 --> 16:32.780
If I'd only known, I could have
 put something in my onigiri!

16:32.780 --> 16:34.740
Right, Sengoku? 
Like shiso leaves or something!

16:34.740 --> 16:37.230
Huh? Sh-Sh-Shiso?

16:38.340 --> 16:40.020
Are those middle schoolers?

16:42.730 --> 16:46.660
S-So you all showed up to 
school early? That's so dumb!

16:46.660 --> 16:49.270
I'm just glad it wasn't just me.

16:49.270 --> 16:53.700
Our teacher made a point of saying that
 prospective students were coming today.

16:53.700 --> 16:56.480
Oh, so that's why there were 
middle schoolers wandering around.

16:56.480 --> 16:57.780
Yep, that's right.

16:57.780 --> 17:00.110
Where are Miyamura and Yuki?

17:00.570 --> 17:02.660
They went to buy something to drink.

17:03.270 --> 17:05.190
Now, why are you here early, Hori?

17:05.190 --> 17:06.680
Oh, that's because...

17:07.460 --> 17:08.630
Kyon-Kyon!

17:10.060 --> 17:12.050
Ready to hit the school store?

17:12.520 --> 17:13.620
You bet I am.

17:14.660 --> 17:16.110
We can buy whatever we want!

17:16.590 --> 17:25.190
<b>Squee
Squee
Squee</b>

17:17.850 --> 17:20.370
I get it. There won't be 
any lines in the cafeteria.

17:21.100 --> 17:23.290
Wanna go get lunch?

17:23.290 --> 17:24.480
Sure!

17:28.870 --> 17:31.120
There's more middle schoolers.

17:32.110 --> 17:33.900
I wonder if there are lots of 'em.

17:33.900 --> 17:38.450
I dunno. I can't get over 
how young they look.

17:38.790 --> 17:40.330
Say, is your sister coming?

17:40.330 --> 17:44.450
Not a chance. She hates being in groups.

17:44.950 --> 17:47.270
If she is here, she'd be on her own—

17:47.270 --> 17:51.460
Um, I think we're somewhere around here.

17:51.460 --> 17:54.960
<i>Kitahara!</i>

17:53.430 --> 17:54.960
What's wrong, Shu?!

17:55.520 --> 17:58.510
Get moving, body!

17:58.510 --> 17:59.970
Is something bothering you?

17:59.970 --> 18:01.760
Um, excuse me.

18:01.760 --> 18:02.470
Huh?

18:02.780 --> 18:04.060
We seem to be lost.

18:05.870 --> 18:07.200
Where do you want to go?

18:07.200 --> 18:11.260
We're supposed to meet up here,
 at the edge of the field.

18:11.260 --> 18:14.730
Ah, you can get there faster
 from the side entrance.

18:15.520 --> 18:20.410
Follow this hall, go down the stairs
 to the right, and you'll end up outside.

18:20.790 --> 18:22.240
Thank you.

18:22.240 --> 18:24.190
Hey, Shu!

18:24.190 --> 18:26.750
<i>Don't call my name! Why would you do that?!</i>

18:28.250 --> 18:30.500
<b>Doesn't know 
Iura's
full name</b>

18:30.500 --> 18:32.280
What's with him?

18:32.280 --> 18:34.860
Anyway, thank you again.

18:34.860 --> 18:36.760
Sure. Take care now.

18:38.780 --> 18:40.200
He's finally leaving.

18:40.770 --> 18:42.510
What are you doing?

18:42.850 --> 18:45.890
C'mon, Iura-kun, let's go!

18:45.890 --> 18:48.770
Once lunch break starts, it'll get crowded!

18:48.770 --> 18:51.020
<i>Ayasaki-san!</i>

18:51.020 --> 18:53.050
Iura-kun, c'mon!

18:53.450 --> 18:54.770
What's wrong, Kitahara?

18:54.770 --> 18:57.760
<i>Why is a girl calling my name
 now of all times?</i>

18:57.760 --> 19:00.580
Hey! Earth to Iura-kun!

19:00.580 --> 19:03.350
<i>But if I move, Kitahara will see me!</i>

19:01.270 --> 19:04.190
Earth to Iura-kun!

19:03.350 --> 19:05.790
<i>I'm sorry, Ayasaki-san! Go on without me!</i>

19:04.710 --> 19:05.790
Iura-kun?

19:06.460 --> 19:08.160
Iura, hurry up.

19:08.160 --> 19:10.730
Oh, right. I'm sorry.

19:08.160 --> 19:11.670
<b>Pressure</b>

19:11.670 --> 19:12.670
Huh?

19:16.170 --> 19:17.510
You're...

19:18.330 --> 19:19.670
Senpai?

19:19.670 --> 19:21.860
<i>"Senpai," huh?</i>

19:21.860 --> 19:26.560
<i>If he'd called me anything else,
I would've pretended not to know him!</i>

19:27.090 --> 19:29.060
Senpai, I...

19:29.740 --> 19:32.970
<i>It's hard to pretend I don't know
him when he calls me that...</i>

19:32.970 --> 19:33.990
<i>Scram already!</i>

19:39.320 --> 19:42.060
H-Hey, you're supposed to be outside!

19:42.060 --> 19:43.720
Get going!

19:44.820 --> 19:45.870
Ow!

19:44.820 --> 19:48.080
<i>WHACK</i>

19:45.870 --> 19:48.080
Why are you bullying him, Iura?!

19:48.640 --> 19:51.380
Don't go around scaring middle schoolers!

19:51.380 --> 19:54.460
They're way more scared of you, Yasuda.

19:57.070 --> 19:58.540
Do you know Iura?

19:59.180 --> 20:01.950
Do you go to Iura's middle school?

20:01.950 --> 20:05.720
Um, does he have a girlfriend?

20:09.310 --> 20:12.100
<i>S-Stifled giggles and sympathy...</i>

20:12.100 --> 20:15.650
What do we say? That he does?

20:15.650 --> 20:17.980
Let's respect his wishes.

20:18.290 --> 20:19.730
<i>I feel even more pathetic!</i>

20:19.980 --> 20:23.940
That's enough. You're leaving!

20:25.590 --> 20:27.740
Care to join us at the school store?

20:27.740 --> 20:29.490
No!

20:30.470 --> 20:33.490
We have to go back to school for lunch.

20:33.490 --> 20:34.620
Oh.

20:34.620 --> 20:35.620
Phew.

20:36.290 --> 20:37.780
Is that a relief?

20:37.780 --> 20:40.740
You're freaking me out today. Leave already.

20:41.130 --> 20:42.260
Senpai—

20:41.580 --> 20:45.270
Okay, okay, you guys quit
lollygagging and get going.

20:45.810 --> 20:49.740
I'll take you where you 
need to go, so follow me.

20:49.740 --> 20:51.470
Y-Yes, sir.

20:51.470 --> 20:54.640
Yasuda, you should be nice to us, too.

20:54.640 --> 20:58.530
Why's that? You're never nice to me.

20:58.530 --> 20:59.960
Aw...

21:00.800 --> 21:03.140
<i>Yasuda, thank you.</i>

21:02.690 --> 21:05.660
<b>The first time Iura's
ever thanked Yasuda</b>

21:05.660 --> 21:08.160
Peach Tea

21:07.280 --> 21:08.160
Aw!

21:08.750 --> 21:11.910
I would have liked to see that!

21:11.910 --> 21:13.940
Me too, me too!

21:13.940 --> 21:17.650
Huh? Why? It wasn't funny at all.

21:17.650 --> 21:19.420
Sure it was.

21:19.750 --> 21:22.790
You were acting the part of his senpai!

21:22.790 --> 21:26.000
Wh-What's wrong with that? 
Nothing, that's what!

21:26.000 --> 21:29.570
But you don't usually react
 to people so negatively.

21:29.570 --> 21:30.730
Are you on bad terms?

21:30.730 --> 21:33.680
That boy seemed comfortable around him.

21:33.680 --> 21:36.490
He's in the same class as my sister.

21:36.490 --> 21:38.800
He just happened to be here today.

21:38.800 --> 21:41.570
What? They you you should try
to get along with him!

21:41.570 --> 21:43.580
Well, y'know...

21:43.580 --> 21:46.240
What? Why are you being so wishy-washy?

21:46.240 --> 21:48.390
Is there something else about him—

21:50.860 --> 21:52.950
Was it him? Is he the one?

21:54.980 --> 21:56.620
He is, isn't he?!

21:56.620 --> 21:58.510
Aw, I didn't get to see him!

21:58.510 --> 21:59.870
Me neither!

21:59.870 --> 22:02.810
Shu, is that true? For real?

22:05.530 --> 22:08.040
Who is this middle schooler?

22:08.040 --> 22:09.240
No idea.

23:36.390 --> 23:39.900
Next time
page.6 Sleepover
